<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f76c7e05c11313d30e8d7067d1e8d931963f44093b88ccbdc62e92e4efa39c5</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>VW scraps production modernization plan citing tough financial straits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:578a2add35843bb95d9807dca4e9e109a6f8b163cfdcbf9a01d120999b5e062e</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597--b06c676e46e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">VW has announced that it will scrap large-scale modernization in light of its current economic situation. Employee representatives accuse leadership of putting short-term profits before long-term company viability.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Only 1/3 of Germans satisfied with state of democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:061aa1ad6e5f044107369c1b12cbc176485c940270f0eef4f816ec22a71370e3</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066--348a315bae46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new authoritarianism study has revealed a new low in satisfaction levels with the functioning of German democracy. Meanwhile, the Bundeswehr has banned Chinese-made drones. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Ilse Aigner meets parties at Bundestag</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2002d26919390242377293d6d5c4bc7dc5be696cf49facf56908fd0db9e599f</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ilse-aigner-meets-parties-at-bundestag/live-79906440--d4a05b14149e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ilse-aigner-meets-parties-at-bundestag/live-79906440?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ilse Aigner said she wouldn't meet with the far-right AfD. Meanwhile, Chancellor Merz is set to host Hungarian Prime Minister Magyar.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Integration of immigrants in Germany: Much has been accomplished but problems remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3837a9e6681025a1396f5291810f698b1ea0cf16489df9443da49b96bbe9afaa</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241--cdefd1e9fff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Federal office for Migration and Refugees has released a new Integration Report. It found that while the integration of people with a migrant history is improving, violent youth remain a problem.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Democracy study: One-quarter of Germans want a right-wing authoritarian dictatorship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ac1a41556b96c78ec6ae1b97599faeacfca86d0e4fbd2889bc408f5eb07cbf2</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718--e6377f13d887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's electoral successes point to a new trend in Germany: Prejudice, resentment, and extremism are on the rise. A new study suggests satisfaction with democracy is at a low ebb.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8b689b830b9c5f19a029dc3e754cd4e2eecf6afe9d2aa587630d2b78b64ef63</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
